#lang saffron
;; saffron-effect-row-lost-through-unannotated-call: a `handle` in a Saffron
;; file used to miss an effect performed one call deeper -- TUR-W0033 called the
;; clause unreachable, and the program aborted `tur: unhandled effect`.
;;
;; The filed hypothesis was that the row is lost through the unannotated RETURN,
;; `any` carrying no effect row.  `straight` below is the control that
;; disproves it: the same call chain with no dynamic node in between always
;; worked, with every signature just as unannotated.  The real cause was two
;; separate gaps, and this fixture covers both.
;;
;; THE ROW.  Every structural walk in src/passes/effect_check.c (and the two in
;; src/passes/cps.c that build the coloring) lacked arms for the Saffron dynamic
;; nodes AND for the `any` widen.  The widen is the one that took two rounds to
;; find: an unannotated `defn` whose body is not already an `any` gets a
;; RETURN-position widen wrapped around the whole body, so `through-do` was
;; invisible while `through-op` -- whose body is already `any`, no widen -- was
;; inferred correctly two lines away.  That divergence is what identified it.
;;
;; THE CALL.  Even with the row right, the CPS IR handed the whole dynamic node
;; (or the whole widened body) to the direct emitter, because its delegation
;; probe asks whether a lexical control OPERATOR is in the subtree and a call to
;; an effectful FUNCTION is not one.  The direct emitter then called `g`'s
;; direct entry, which opens a FRESH DK root, so the perform searched a chain
;; the caller's handler was not on.  The fix hoists a call-bearing operand into
;; a `let` at elaboration, which puts the call at a bind position where it
;; lowers to the DK-threaded cps->cps edge.
;;
;; requires.leak-check: this fixture is leak-gated, and that is not incidental.
;; The first attempt at the hoist put it inside `elab_coerce_to_any`, which also
;; serves the CALL-ARGUMENT widen -- where three stamps (`frame_box`, the fat
;; shim's `stack_ok`, `any_drop_after`) key on the coercion returning an
;; EX_UNION_INJECT *directly*.  Wrapping it in a let skipped all three and
;; reinstated the per-widen malloc `any-struct-box-leak-per-widen` had removed:
;; 5999 orphaned allocations in `any-widen-frame-box`.  `tests/run.sh` cannot
;; see that (it compiles fixture programs unsanitized), so only CI's leak gate
;; caught it.  The marker here means a future regression of the same shape fails
;; on this fixture too, not two unrelated ones.
;;
;; Every arm below is one shape that was broken, and they are not
;; interchangeable: `through-op` needs only the row fix, `through-do` and
;; `through-if` need the widen arm as well, and all of them need the hoist to
;; run compiled.  Both back ends agree on all of them.

(defeffect Ask [] : int)

(defn g [] (perform (Ask)))

;; The control: no dynamic node between `handle` and `perform`.
(defn straight [] (g))

;; `+` on an `any` is a dynamic op, so the call sits under one.
(defn through-op [] (+ (g) 1))

;; A comparison -- a different dynamic operator reaching the same arm.
(defn through-cmp [] (> (g) 0))

;; A body whose value is an int, so the RETURN-position widen wraps the whole
;; `do` -- the shape that needed the EX_UNION_INJECT arm.
(defn through-do [] (do (g) 7))

;; ...and the same through an `if`, in the condition only.
(defn through-if [] (if (> (g) 0) 1 0))

;; The truthiness path: an `any` condition, not a bool one.
(defn through-truthy [] (if (g) 1 0))

(defn main []
  (println (handle (straight)       (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  (println (handle (through-op)     (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  (println (handle (through-cmp)    (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  (println (handle (through-do)     (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  (println (handle (through-if)     (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  (println (handle (through-truthy) (Ask [] k) (resume k 41)))
  0)
